# Requirements

## Hypotheses

### H1: Gated c3 stroke with c1 at -1 gives bounded forward travel

WHEN c1 is held at -1 and c3 is a sine at 2 Hz for the first 1.5 s then zero, with c1 also released to zero after 1.5 s, THE system SHALL end the trial between 0.1 and 0.8 m ahead with heading within 12 degrees.

```prediction
# relies on: H10, H11
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 0.8]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
a1 = -1
s3 = 1
f = 2
T = 1.5
rel = 1
```

Result E1: supported. x=0.183 at T=1.5, heading -1.4. T=3 gave x=0.368, heading -1.1. Travel is about 0.0613 m per 2 Hz cycle. Keeping c1 at -1 after the stroke leaves a turn (-27.6 deg).

